"party":"Centre Alliance","person_id":"tvfy_10874","person_slug":"rebekha-sharkie","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Rick Wilson","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10816","person_slug":"rick-wilson","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Rob Mitchell","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10733","person_slug":"rob-mitchell","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Sally Sitou","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10995","person_slug":"sally-sitou","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Sam Birrell","party":"Nationals","person_id":"tvfy_10991","person_slug":"sam-birrell","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Sam Lim","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_11000","person_slug":"sam-lim","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Sam Rae","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10982","person_slug":"sam-rae","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Sharon Claydon","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10805","person_slug":"sharon-claydon","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Shayne Neumann","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10485","person_slug":"shayne-neumann","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Sophie Scamps","party":"Independent","person_id":"tvfy_10989","person_slug":"sophie-scamps","vote":"no"},{"name":"Stephen Bates","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10970","person_slug":"stephen-bates","vote":"no"},{"name":"Stephen Jones","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10740","person_slug":"stephen-jones","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Steve Georganas","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10245","person_slug":"steve-georganas","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Susan Templeman","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10873","person_slug":"susan-templeman","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Tania Lawrence","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10981","person_slug":"tania-lawrence","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Terry Young","party":"LNP","person_id":"tvfy_10933","person_slug":"terry-young","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Tim Watts","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10794","person_slug":"tim-watts","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Tony Burke","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10081","person_slug":"tony-burke","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Tony Pasin","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10784","person_slug":"tony-pasin","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Tony Zappia","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10695","person_slug":"tony-zappia","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Tracey Roberts","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10994","person_slug":"tracey-roberts","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Zali Steggall","party":"Independent","person_id":"tvfy_10941","person_slug":"zali-steggall","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Zaneta Mascarenhas","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10999","person_slug":"zaneta-mascarenhas","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Zoe Daniel","party":"Independent","person_id":"tvfy_10979","person_slug":"zoe-daniel","vote":"aye"}],"name":"Anti-Discrimination and Human Rights Legislation Amendment (Respect at Work) Bill 2022 - Consideration in Detail - Equal-access approach","noes":9,"question":"The majority voted in favour of *disagreeing* with [amendments](https://www.openaustralia.org.au/debate/?id=2022-11-07.120.1) introduced by Kooyong MP [Monique Ryan](https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/people/representatives/kooyong/monique_ryan) (Independent), which means they failed and won't be included in the bill. ### What did the amendments do? Dr Ryan [explained that](https://www.openaustralia.org.au/debate/?id=2022-11-07.120.1): > *The Respect@Work report proposed that costs might be ordered against the applicant only where the court was satisfied that the party instituted the proceedings vexatiously or without cause. That model has not been adopted in this bill. Instead, this bill proposes a cost-neutrality approach in which litigants bear their own costs unless the court orders otherwise. The bill does set out various factors that the court must have regard to in making costs orders. Superficially, the cost-neutral arrangement represents an improvement on the status quo. In effect, however, its design and the uncertainty around its operation will serve to undermine access to justice by limiting the ability of applicants to secure legal representation. Taking a cost-neutrality approach to a relationship characterised by systemic inequality only serves to entrench that inequality.* > > *The amendment I have proposed offers an alternative: an equal-access approach. Under this proposal, each party will bear its own costs, except when the applicant is unsuccessful—that is, when the court has found that the respondent has engaged in discriminatory conduct, in which case the respondent will be liable to pay the applicant's costs, as they should. You should not be excused from bearing costs when you have broken the law. People and organisations found to have engaged in discrimination or harassment in breach of the law should have to pay the legal costs of the applicant. This will act as an incentive to change workplace cultures that permit discriminatory treatment. This","result":"affirmative","slug":"division-federal-representatives-7822","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/representatives/2022-11-07/7"}
